# 15. Governance Document Lifecycle

## Purpose

This section establishes the lifecycle governing the Objective Governance document itself.

Its purpose is to ensure that this document evolves through a controlled, transparent, and traceable engineering process while preserving repository integrity and governance continuity.

---

## Lifecycle Principles

The lifecycle of this governance document shall:

- Preserve engineering authority.
- Maintain complete revision history.
- Support controlled evolution.
- Protect governance stability.
- Ensure continuous improvement.

---

## Lifecycle Stages

### Stage 1 — Draft

The document is being developed and has not yet received formal engineering approval.

---

### Stage 2 — Under Review

The document is undergoing engineering and governance review.

Comments, recommendations, and corrections shall be evaluated before approval.

---

### Stage 3 — Approved Baseline

The document has been formally approved and becomes the governing baseline for objective governance.

---

### Stage 4 — Active

The approved document is in active use within the AVIA repository.

---

### Stage 5 — Revision

Approved modifications are incorporated following the established governance process.

Every revision shall preserve historical traceability.

---

### Stage 6 — Superseded

A newer approved version replaces the current document.

The superseded version remains archived for historical reference.

---

### Stage 7 — Archived

The document is retained solely as an engineering record and is no longer active within the repository.

---

## Lifecycle Transition Rules

Transitions between lifecycle stages shall:

- Be formally documented.
- Receive appropriate approval.
- Preserve document history.
- Maintain version traceability.
- Update repository records where required.

---

## Lifecycle Records

The lifecycle history of this document shall record:

- Document version.
- Lifecycle stage.
- Date of transition.
- Engineering rationale.
- Approval reference.
- Related revisions.

---

## Engineering Perspective

Governance documents are engineering artifacts.

They require the same discipline, traceability, and controlled evolution expected of the objectives they govern.

Managing governance documents through a defined lifecycle ensures that the governance framework itself remains reliable, transparent, and adaptable throughout the evolution of the AVIA project.
